{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1095188-what-if-people-knew","id":1095188,"title":"What if people knew?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-21T11:41:50-07:00","id":1095188,"title":"What if people knew?","content":"How could the world suddenly be exposed to the fact that the Fae existed and what would be the fallout?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T11:59:11-07:00","id":1095195,"title":"","content":"Do you mean like a Mass Scale Permanent Enchantment or more like everyone was Suddenly aware that all the Stories about Faeries were Real and that they never left but still can't see them properly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3239-jane_dargason","name":"Jane_Dargason","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3239_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T12:02:40-07:00","id":1095197,"title":"","content":"The latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T12:07:32-07:00","id":1095200,"title":"","content":"The Mists would kick in and/or Banality would undo the Dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T12:08:25-07:00","id":1095201,"title":"","content":"Because people know? People knew before the Mists kicked in and there are people who believe today.<br /> <br /> Edit: It's more of a sense that something is confirmed as being out there, and it seems to be connected to the old stories of centuries past. It could be mutants, a series of well hidden cousins to humanity or even aliens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 05-21-2017, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T23:53:18-07:00","id":1095390,"title":"","content":"One of my apocalypse Scenarios is the world discovering the Supernatural exist by some public Vampire incident. The result being bigger then the Resurgence and the Fomorians and Tuatha stirring and the Gates of Arcadia blasting wide open as Magic returns to the World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T10:12:54-07:00","id":1095533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1095188-what-if-people-knew?p=1095390#post1095390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my apocalypse Scenarios is the world discovering the Supernatural exist by some public Vampire incident. The result being bigger then the Resurgence and the Fomorians and Tuatha stirring and the Gates of Arcadia blasting wide open as Magic returns to the World.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adventure Time! Come on and Grab your friends, We'll go to very Distant Lands...<br /> <br /> Sorry, I couldn't resist. But Honestly I think that Humans knowing and Accepting that the Fae are Real and live among them would cause something like the Resurgence on Crack and would probably wake the Fomorians and Tuatha or at least bring about the return of Firstborn if you decide that DA: Fae is part of the same continuity","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3239-jane_dargason","name":"Jane_Dargason","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3239_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T14:25:43-07:00","id":1095619,"title":"","content":"Aye I do. How would you imagine firstborn, true Fae, and Tuatha powers would differ from changelings. I imagine they would be more sensitive to Banality and Cold Iron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T16:44:28-07:00","id":1095656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1095188-what-if-people-knew?p=1095619#post1095619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aye I do. How would you imagine firstborn, true Fae, and Tuatha powers would differ from changelings. I imagine they would be more sensitive to Banality and Cold Iron.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Firstborn I'd to with them counting permanently having called Upon the Wyrd active and not suffering Imbalance from Unleashings, though Unleashings would still be as chaotic and unpredictable as always, while gaining Imbalance, and so Nightmare, from utilicing the more predictable and stable Cantrips. And I would probably make them to have Echoes at maxlevel without recompense. All of them would also be extremely vulnerable to Banality especially if not hiding their nature through Magic or by Calling Upon the Autumn, latter of which would likely inflict automatic Banality but could save one from gaining even more by exposure. Not sure of the exact mechanics I would use but possibly having some Banality triggers inflict automatic Banality instead of being able to &quot;soak&quot; it with Glamour.<br /> <br /> But these are just from the top of my head ideas without thinking much of balance but rather focusing on the idea that they are Fae unshielded by any Banal shells and that they are the masters of Unleashings as per DA: Fae.<br /> <br /> And I'd say that they are the so called true Fae as said in DA: Fae. <br /> <br /> Tuatha, and the Fomorians, are a tier above the Kithain and so their mechanics could differ quite a bit from Changelings and for them I have no fast ideas or solutions. I'd say it depended on what your Chronicle needed them to represent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T17:54:01-07:00","id":1095686,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Changelings would suddenly find a saucer of milk on every porch like in the old days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T10:26:15-07:00","id":1095959,"title":"","content":"If we don't consider some sort of mass enchantment or Mists failing to their work and that people start to truly believe, rather than just &quot;Oh, I heard this theory and it's not terribly convincing&quot; (because that's what Mists do - remove or hide all the evidence of Dreaming and its creatures ever existing), then the only for that to work..<br /> <br /> Humanity has to fall back into new dark ages or totalitarian medieval sect, that brainwashes citizens from early childhood into believing, that faeries exist and walk amongst them in human skin. Such society will have the same distribution of Banality and Glamour if not worse and unlucky Changelings will be forced to deal with Banal fanatics, that seek them and know what to look for. They'll probably hate fae, but I'm not sure, that it would be much better, if they were worshipped in this scenario. Smothered in adoration... Urgh. So, yeah, that. <br /> <br /> If you talking about something closer to &quot;Oh, I heard this theory and it's not terribly convincing&quot;, then that would mean someone blatantly shared all the secrets of the changelings (like starting a new movie trend, writing a series of bestseller novels, RPG, etc.). <br /> <br /> Many probably wouldn't know or notice. Majority of exposed would stop thinking about that after a while, but won't forget. There will be small, devoted community, if changelings will be unlucky - it'll hijacked be militant vocal minority, that'll attack anyone for criticizing their chosen work of fiction. It will spawn some fanfiction, ponies and sex might be involved at some point. Consindering the subject, it might fuel or even popularize neo-paganism, animism, otherkin beliefs. Some new followers will be genuinely paganistic, most will be teenagers and 'poseurs'. <br /> <br /> There will be ton of critics, that will take apart the history and society of Changelings. Though, whether they will be or not remembered largely depends on how successful was the original work.<br /> <br /> Of course, there will be merchandize. A lot of it.<br /> <br /> I'm here considering how changelings can be exposed realistically. If say, it's a public document posted on a web it'll go stray to conspiracy therists and relative obscurity<br /> <br /> What's more important... in all cases, kithain gain some very situational benefits here and there. While their enemies will get some real and tangible grasp of their society, powers and weaknessess. Dauntain, mortal hunters, supernatural creatures and even autumn people will get a lot of ammunition to combat kithain. They'll know how to defend themselves, when to attack and how to hide. <br /> <br /> Of course, it's assuming, that Changling won't adapt. But they'll have to for those very reasons I described above. They'll have to find an originator of the leak and take creative control to avoid that kind of scenario, if possible. If not they'll have to transform their society to capitalize on this and avoid uncomfortable questions. Maybe even help to publish similar works, to create sort of &quot;noise&quot;, making it impossible to discern truth. The idea of changelings as a concept being popular in the same way, as superheroes and vampires, might be turned into net positive, if not too many sensitive secrets are exposed.<br /> <br /> On the other hands, with the a halp from Mists, Changelings are the only specie potentially capable of avoiding ill-rumored &quot;Streisand Effect&quot;. <br /> <br /> Probably there might be other factors, I haven't thought. If history was easily predictable, we would've been a different specie. History is consequences stacked, canceling each other, competing, being foiled by random disasters and windfalls and completely unforseen patterns.<br /> <br /> If we consider scenarios, where Mists fail or even disappear completely, that'll be different story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T12:29:15-07:00","id":1095999,"title":"","content":"the actions directly by humans wouldnt be as dangerous as what the garou or cainites or even mages could expect... but banality could even things out...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T13:21:19-07:00","id":1096013,"title":"","content":"The Mists are the single most effective &quot;Masquerade&quot; in the Entire WOD if people some how started believing en masse in fairies then they'd have long since discovered everyone else. I imagine it would be something like Shadowrun..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}